hint: Start the stack with the root, unless the tree is empty.
hint: Loop while the stack isn't empty: `pop()` a node and append its value.
hint: Push its right child, then its left child, each only if it exists.
right: Every node is pushed once and popped once: O(n). Pushing the right child first makes the left subtree come off the stack first.
